config BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_UCM_CONF
	bool "alsa-ucm-conf"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_LIB
	help
	  ALSA Use Case Manager (UCM) configuration — the "ucm2" tree
	  that alsa-lib reads at runtime from /usr/share/alsa/ucm2 to
	  describe a sound card's profiles, jacks and devices.

	  PipeWire / WirePlumber need it to build the real card profiles.
	  Without it the ALSA monitor exposes only a single generic
	  "Analog Stereo" profile, so an HDA card's HDMI/Display outputs
	  never appear as sinks (the N100's monitor speakers were
	  unreachable). Not shipped by Buildroot 2026.08 — this is a
	  PengyOS from-source data recipe.

	  https://github.com/alsa-project/alsa-ucm-conf
